          heading: "German language requirements & courses",
          html: `<p>Foreign students in English-taught master programs have to prove basic knowledge of German language, at the latest after their first year of studies. This requirement is fulfilled if you present either an <strong>A2 certificate of the Goethe Institute</strong> (dating back no more than 1 year) or <strong>complete an A1 course at RPTU</strong>. Further, many departments grant credits for successful participation in higher level German language courses at the university.</p>
          <p>To give you the opportunity to fulfill these requirements and to facilitate your studies and daily life, ISGS offers integrated intensive language courses, the so-called <strong>O.K.: Orientation course</strong> — a combination of an intensive language course, special cultural and social program, excursions, industrial visits, as well as administrative support services.</p>
          <p>At the beginning of the course you take a placement test. According to your results, you'll be organized into several groups with different levels, ranging from beginners (A1) to students with advanced knowledge (A2 or B1) of German. The level is completed after successfully passing the exam. Level exams are offered twice a year (February and July).</p>
          <p><strong>PhD students</strong> do not have to prove knowledge of German language, but are welcomed to take part in the orientation course to facilitate their daily and academic life.</p>`
